From 6304a7441014d8d836ccdcf9677eda5163543528 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cycles Houdini engine authoring <engine@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 04:39:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 97/98] Precompute subdivision edge factors in parallel

DiagSplit::split_patches splits every face serially, and most of its time
goes to edge factors: each T() evaluates the patch at several points along
an edge. With millions of faces this serial pass dominates tessellation,
while dicing is already parallel.

T() depends only on its arguments (patch, parameter range, depth and
resolve mode). Split batches of faces speculatively in parallel first, each
range of faces with its own edges and without allocating subpatches, and
record the arguments and result of every T() call per face. Then split all
faces in order as before; T() returns a recorded result when the arguments
match exactly and computes it otherwise, for example where a neighbouring
face already assigned a shared edge differently. Edges, vertex and triangle
indices, and subpatches are therefore identical to the serial split. The
next batch is precomputed while the current batch is split.

Rationale: Edge factor evaluation in the serial patch split dominated tessellation time for large subdivided meshes on every update.
Contract: Subpatches, edge factors, vertex and triangle indices and the diced mesh are identical to the serial split; errors and limits are reported only by the ordered split.
Tests: tests/houdini_subdivision_smoke.py
---
 src/subd/split.cpp | 131 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 src/subd/split.h   |  22 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 138 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

